WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.440
We talked last week about a poll that showed
that 64 percent of current Republicans are

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:12.730
willing to leave the Republican Party if Donald
Trump were to start a third party.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:20.060
And this reinforced the sort of soft nature
of much of the support of the Republican Party,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:25.990
as well as the cachet that Donald Trump, at
least now as we approach one month since he's

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:32.029
been out of office, that for at least now
Donald Trump still has on the Republican Party.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:33.559
But that is all hypothetical.

00:00:33.559 --> 00:00:37.710
Those are people who would be willing to leave
the Republican Party.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.921
What about people that are leaving and not
because Trump started in another party, but

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:43.050
just because they're leaving?

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:48.790
There is a very interesting series of studies,
many of them out of California, some out of

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:54.329
Florida as well, which show that there are
already thousands and thousands of voters

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:58.039
in some counties that are leaving the Republican
Party.

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:00.940
And what where they are going remains a question.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.840
And we're going to talk about that in a moment.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:10.000
But this seems to be a reaction to the defeat
of Donald Trump, combined with two months

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.369
of lies about the election supposedly having
been stolen from him.

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:20.460
And voting experts at the University of Florida
say that there are thousands and thousands

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:25.529
of Republicans that are no longer traditional
Republicans that are no longer registered

00:01:25.529 --> 00:01:32.880
as Republicans anymore, and that while there
are often changes to party registrations all

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.749
the time, and in particular after elections,
that the number of Republicans leaving the

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:43.880
party are significantly greater in number
than the number of Democrats that are changing

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:44.939
their registrations.

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:50.799
They looked at San Diego County in California,
as well as some other parts of the country,

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:57.280
and it appears as though the January 6th Trump
riot was sort of like the straw that broke

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.319
the camel's back.

00:01:58.319 --> 00:02:04.069
It's unclear that it alone is the explanation
for why so many Republicans are abandoning

00:02:04.069 --> 00:02:10.959
their party, but rather the sort of culmination
to months and really years of a complete joke

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:14.879
of a Republican Party with Donald Trump at
the helm at its head.

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:19.060
And it is believed, indeed, that the abandonment
of the Republican Party by these folks is

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:23.340
a sort of rejection of Trump ism more than
it is of what the Republican Party used to

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.340
be.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.750
These folks who are leaving widely believed
to still be in line with whatever values or

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.810
ideologies brought them in in the first place,
whether it was Ronald Reagan 40 years ago

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:41.019
or whether it was someone like either of the
George Bush's or more the Newt Gingrich style

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:45.620
early 90s politics that attracted people to
the Republican Party or folks like John McCain

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.329
and Mitt Romney, more recent Republican nominees,
whatever it was that brought them.

00:02:49.329 --> 00:02:52.049
And they still they're not leftists.

00:02:52.049 --> 00:02:55.580
They're not leaving because they're leftists,
but they're leaving as a rejection of Trump

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.910
ism is what it seems to be.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:01.299
Now, there's a really important and obvious
question to ask if we want to figure out what

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:06.420
is or is there an electoral impact to this,
which is OK if you leave the Republican Party,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.390
are you still voting for Republicans?

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:12.310
Unless we have reason to believe otherwise,
they probably are.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:16.920
You can leave the Republican Party and be
an independent and still vote just for Republicans.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.980
And I can't imagine that many of these folks
are looking to vote for Democrats at the state

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.360
and local level.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:28.120
Maybe some would stay home, which would still
be a help to the Democratic Party.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:33.030
And sadly, I believe most of these folks will
be very quick to return if indeed what they're

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:38.250
doing is rejecting Trump ism by leaving as
soon as the media focus gets back to Black

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.079
Lives Matter is terrible.

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:44.109
And Joe Biden's allowing immigrants into the
country and owe the debt and the deficit and

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:49.099
all of that tried and true stuff that we predicted
Republicans would go back to after Trump and

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:51.769
that we're already seeing them go back to
after Trump.

00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:53.760
I believe many will return to the party.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:59.430
And importantly, I don't think many of these
folks will opt to vote for Democrats rather

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:05.360
than whatever Republicans they can vote for
in twenty 2022 and in 2024, assuming Donald

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.519
Trump is not the nominee at that point in
time.

00:04:07.519 --> 00:04:12.530
So, you know, you know, independents who used
to be Republicans that still vote for Republicans,

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.340
not super interesting.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:20.109
And it's important to know as a general political
concept, when we talk about independents,

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:25.770
there are some folks who like to frame themselves
as these enlightened centrists that are not

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.560
loyal to either party.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.520
And sometimes they vote for Republicans or
for Democrats or Green Party or whatever.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:38.860
The vast majority of independents vote overwhelmingly
for one party or the other, and they are essentially

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.840
as partizan as most Democrats or Republicans.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.979
They just aren't officially a.

00:04:42.979 --> 00:04:47.639
Affiliated with any party, and let's not overstate.

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:52.520
The importance of party registration alone
now that being said, if a lot of Republicans

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.810
are abandoning the party, if some of them
are saying for the time being, I'm not going

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:00.030
to be donating, these are things that could
make a difference.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.390
The question then becomes, will Democrats
take advantage of it?

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:03.551
And that certainly remains to be seen.

